      ":question/id": "b22f045c-0b9c-53f1-b536-66fda02ca447",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-24361",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={7.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {7.5}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x={15}^{∘},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
