      ":question/id": "91b3ae38-a411-55e5-ba0c-b0976c1d82dd",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-120093",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n\\displaystyle 8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)=\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{32}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right) & =4\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\right]\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right) & =2\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =2\\left[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
