      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/hard"
      },
      ":question/id": "e9ff4e40-981d-5344-8025-a467141eea82",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-364640",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)}.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
