      ":question/id": "c41ea86a-3b09-5773-9843-df888de284a4",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-76664",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n\\displaystyle 6\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)=\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right) & =3\\cdot \\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\right)\\right]\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\right)} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
