      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
      },
      ":question/id": "0abb88c3-b1d8-5fd6-9259-e93980f1b3ad",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n3\\sin(15^\\circ)\\cos(15^\\circ)\\cos(30^\\circ).\n$$",
      ":question/retired": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the double-angle identity in the form $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\sin(15^\\circ)\\cos(15^\\circ)\\cos(30^\\circ)\n&=\\frac{3}{2}\\sin(30^\\circ)\\cos(30^\\circ)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{4}\\sin(60^\\circ)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe identity is used twice: the angles progress from $15^\\circ$ to $30^\\circ$ to $60^\\circ$. Each use introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186696009,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
