      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/hard"
      },
      ":question/id": "1043af1e-be8e-50e8-a088-c079feee421f",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n\\frac{\\sec\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\right)}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{16}\\right)}.\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/retired": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "First use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ in the denominator. Then write secant as the reciprocal of cosine:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sec\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\right)}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{16}\\right)}\n&=\\frac{2\\sec\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\right)}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{4}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe last step uses the double-angle identity a second time. Since $\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$ lies in quadrant III, $\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Therefore,\n$$\n\\frac{4}{-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}=-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2}}=-4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186696011,
