      ":question/id": "4ea294b3-11ab-5619-84a6-dff30ff4752b",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n2\\,\\sin\\left(15^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(15^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/retired": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=15^\\circ$ and then at $x=30^\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
