      ":question/id": "a6d7004b-efb4-5d6a-bc77-0990b992565b",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n6\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right).\n$$\nUse $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ and then with $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
      ":question/retired": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=3\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=1$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\left(1\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
