      ":question/id": "d5d5532c-d9d1-5837-8ecd-a43746e5a051",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right).\n$$\nUse $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ and then with $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.",
      ":question/retired": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
