      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
      },
      ":question/id": "efb73604-909d-53a0-ae97-6e34be06688f",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n3\\,\\sin\\left(7.5^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(7.5^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(15^\\circ\\right).\n$$\nUse $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=7.5^\\circ$ and then with $x=15^\\circ$.",
      ":question/retired": true,
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=7.5^\\circ$ and then at $x=15^\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(15^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(15^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{8}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186749214,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
