      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/hard"
      },
      ":question/id": "0b0c10e5-d9cd-5acf-90f2-1444664f4067",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n\\frac{2\\,\\sec\\left(30^\\circ\\right)}{\\sin\\left(15^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(15^\\circ\\right)}.\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Apply $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ at $x=15^\\circ$ in the denominator. Use $\\sec x=1/\\cos x$, then apply the double-angle identity again at $x=30^\\circ$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{4\\,\\sec\\left(30^\\circ\\right)}{\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)}\\\\&=\\frac{4}{\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)}\\\\&=\\frac{8}{\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\nRationalize the denominator by multiplying numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{3}$:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{8}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)}\\\\&=\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{3}}\\\\&=\\frac{16 \\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    {
