      ":question/id": "34e7eb2c-14af-5bd1-bf04-01774dae2e4c",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n8\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{16}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=4\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=2\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\,\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
