      ":question/id": "90970a95-e0ab-56f8-bcbf-d7ffa043e550",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n4\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\&=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=1$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\left(1\\right)\\\\&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
