      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
      },
      ":question/id": "c5362cd4-e28f-5871-8896-bc4de86ede35",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n\\sin\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{16}$ and then at $x=\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
